// `dbg!(v)` — print an i64 value for debugging and return it unchanged, so it
// can be dropped into any expression: `set x = dbg!(compute())`.
//
// `dasu` is the builtin print function (dispatches on type), so the macro body
// prints the value and returns it. `dbg!` is i64-typed for V1 (a generic
// `dbg!` requires function-level generics, which mire does not yet support);
// for other types call `dasu(v)` directly.

@[macro!] pub fn dbg: (v :i64) :i64 {
    dasu(v)
    return v
}
